  "body": "## What happens\n\nA user tested the tool editor in a build of `main` at `4d891498e`:\n\n- The 3D preview draws helical flutes (#3908) only for basic end mills. Keyseat cutters, dovetail cutters and the other kinds show no flutes.\n- The mesh resolution of the preview is low. Round edges show as visible facets.\n- The holder, the shank and the flutes all have the same grey colour. It is hard to see where the holder ends and the tool starts.\n\n## Expected\n\n- Each tool kind that has flutes shows them in the preview: bull nose, ball nose, chamfer, keyseat, dovetail, tapered, drill, and the others that have a flute length.\n- The revolved mesh uses more segments, so that the round edges look smooth at the size of the preview. Keep the frame time low (for example: more segments only for the preview, not for collision meshes).\n- The holder, the shank and the cutting part (flutes) each get their own theme ink. Use the theme tokens (`crates/ui-kit`), with no colour literals, in dark and light themes.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Reported by the user in chat on 2026-11-27, while testing the tool library refit (U8 to U12, #3663).\n- The thread mill shape is a separate bug: see the P3 issue filed at the same time.\n\n## Done means\n\n- A test for each tool kind with flutes checks that the preview has a flute mesh.\n- The segment count of the preview mesh is higher, and a test pins it.\n- The three parts use three theme inks, and the theme legal and contrast checks pass.\n- Before and after screenshots in the PR.\n- Display only: no change to toolpath, collision, simulation or posted output.\n",
